Add duckdb_fetch_chunk_into: fetch into a caller-owned, reused data chunk

Companion to 0001 (both born from profiling C-API clients against
duckdb-python): duckdb_fetch_chunk allocates a fresh DataChunk per call —
MaterializedQueryResult::FetchInternal's DataChunk::Initialize was ~33% of a
chunk-streaming SELECT's runtime. duckdb_fetch_chunk_into scans the collection
directly into a caller-provided chunk instead:

  - MaterializedQueryResult::FetchInto(DataChunk&): FetchInternal minus the
    allocation, sharing the same scan cursor.
  - duckdb_fetch_chunk_into(result, chunk): C wrapper; for non-materialized
    results falls back to Fetch + DataChunk::Reference (correct, no alloc win).

Note for upstreaming: duckdb.h is autogenerated by scripts/generate_c_api.py;
this patch edits the generated header directly, an upstream PR must add the
definition to src/include/duckdb/main/capi/header_generation/ instead.

diff --git a/src/include/duckdb.h b/src/include/duckdb.h
index dad9dd0..24fe0a6 100644
--- a/src/include/duckdb.h
+++ b/src/include/duckdb.h
@@ -6699,6 +6699,19 @@ DUCKDB_C_API duckdb_result_type duckdb_result_return_type(duckdb_result result);
  * @return duckdb_data_chunk
  */
 DUCKDB_C_API duckdb_data_chunk duckdb_fetch_chunk(duckdb_result result);
+
+/*!
+Fetches the next data chunk into an existing chunk, reusing its buffers. The chunk must match the result's column
+types. Each call overwrites its contents; the caller retains ownership.
+
+For materialized results this scans directly into the chunk. Other result types fall back to fetching and referencing
+the returned buffers.
+
+* @param result The result to fetch from.
+* @param chunk The caller-owned destination chunk.
+* @return true if a chunk was fetched, false when exhausted or on error.
+*/
+DUCKDB_C_API bool duckdb_fetch_chunk_into(duckdb_result result, duckdb_data_chunk chunk);
 #endif

 #if DUCKDB_API_VERSION_AT_LEAST(1, 5, 6)
diff --git a/src/include/duckdb/main/materialized_query_result.hpp b/src/include/duckdb/main/materialized_query_result.hpp
index f656a07..6aeacf1 100644
--- a/src/include/duckdb/main/materialized_query_result.hpp
+++ b/src/include/duckdb/main/materialized_query_result.hpp
@@ -52,6 +52,10 @@ public:
 	//! Takes ownership of the collection, 'collection' is null after this operation
 	unique_ptr<ColumnDataCollection> TakeCollection();

+	//! Fetch the next chunk into an existing DataChunk, reusing its buffers instead of allocating a
+	//! fresh chunk per call. Shares the scan cursor with Fetch. Returns false when the scan is exhausted.
+	DUCKDB_API bool FetchInto(DataChunk &result);
+
 protected:
 	DUCKDB_API unique_ptr<DataChunk> FetchInternal() override;

